      "math_academy_id": "e-12973",
      "problem": "Calculate the value of $50 \\div (-5).$",
      "worked_solution": "We have to divide a positive number $\\color{blue}(50)$ by a negative one $\\color{red}(-5).$ So the result will be negative:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14147219/assets/b60e5b61abd8610de7dd17c7cf2b306fad99db1eae23b2daee61cffc0a54bdb8.svg)\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $50$ by $5$ without any signs: $50 \\div 5 = 10.$ Therefore,  we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}{50}} \\div {\\color{red}{(-5)}} = {\\color{red}{-10}}.\n$$",
